1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:03,750
It's seven in the morning and these people
have been walking since midnight.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,350
13 kilometres along the coast of Kerala,
praying the rosary without ever stopping.

3
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:16,850
In 1647 a statue of Saint Sebastian
arrives from Milan.

4
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:19,250
The world, told by those who live it.

5
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,900
This is Voci Vere.

6
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:25,750
It's called Akhanda Japamala, the unbroken
rosary.

7
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:28,600
It starts from a shrine dedicated to Mary,
in Kalavoor,

8
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,800
and it ends in Arthunkal.

9
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:33,900
13 kilometres along the coast, and the
prayer never stops.

10
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:38,400
I'm on the coast of the Indian Ocean, in
Kerala.

11
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:42,650
One of the most famous pilgrimages in
India is about to begin.

12
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:47,950
Millions of people gathered, walking tens
of kilometres

13
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:52,300
along the coast, to reach the Basilica of
Saint Andrew.

14
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:54,250
All of this from midnight.

15
00:00:57,880 --> 00:01:01,650
A community that gathers to walk in
devotion

16
00:01:02,170 --> 00:01:03,150
to the Blessed Virgin.

17
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:09,200
And the local people will prepare food and
drinks to give to the pilgrims.

18
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,900
No one would have guessed it would fill up
during the night.

19
00:01:21,810 --> 00:01:23,850
We set off in the dark, no one talks about
anything else.

20
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,650
Whoever leads the rosary says the first
half of the prayer. The others answer.

21
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:28,900
For kilometres.

22
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:32,150
The prayer passes from one group to the
next, without a gap.

23
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,450
Hundreds of thousands of people.

24
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,450
The first time, in 2002, there were a few
hundred.

25
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:46,400
As they told us, it starts from a shrine
dedicated to Mary, in Kalavoor.

26
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:49,700
They used to do it all on the road, but
with the traffic

27
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:53,000
it got too chaotic, so they moved straight
onto the beach.

28
00:01:53,770 --> 00:01:55,400
Some come for faith, some for a promise,

29
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:56,900
some because their father did it before
them.

30
00:01:57,390 --> 00:01:58,800
The road is the same for everyone.

31
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:00,950
What does it mean for you?

32
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,100
So this is basically a rally which happens
every year.

33
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:07,600
It's based on the apparition of Mother
Mary

34
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,200
which happened in Alappuzha.

35
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,700
It happened in December 2004,

36
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:13,700
December seventh, I guess,

37
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:17,700
at 2:30 in the afternoon: an apparition of
Mother Mary.

38
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:24,700
October is the month of the Rosary, for
Mother Mary.

39
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,500
We celebrate it with a big rally.

40
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,400
It ends at the Basilica of Saint Andrew.

41
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:35,950
Since October is the month of Mother Mary,
we dedicate this month to the rally.

42
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:39,450
And about four lakh people take part in
it.

43
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:40,500
How many people?

44
00:02:40,550 --> 00:02:42,300
Four lakh. Close to four lakh.

45
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,650
Can you tell me why you do it?

46
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:52,450
It's like a prayer to Jesus, my love.

47
00:02:52,650 --> 00:02:54,450
It's like... for one year.

48
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:55,950
One time.

49
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,050
Why do you come back every year?

50
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:05,700
For Mother Mary.

51
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:06,900
We always come.

52
00:03:06,950 --> 00:03:08,600
There are Christians...

53
00:03:08,650 --> 00:03:09,300
Yes.

54
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:12,600
Muslims. All together.

55
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:16,700
Is it the first time for you here?

56
00:03:17,850 --> 00:03:18,400
What's your name?

57
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:19,700
Elizabeth.

58
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:21,400
What does it mean for you?

59
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:25,100
It's just like giving a devotion to Mother
Mary.

60
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:28,700
She has given me a lot of blessings in my
life.

61
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:30,250
Through Jesus Christ.

62
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:32,200
So you are a Christian, of course.

63
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:34,700
You are Christian. Yes.

64
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,000
How old are you?

65
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:37,100
Twenty-six.

66
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:38,350
This is the first time here.

67
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:40,200
Are you from Kerala?

68
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:43,750
I'm from Malappuram.

69
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:47,750
And for you, is it the first time?

70
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:48,450
No.

71
00:03:48,950 --> 00:03:49,950
We walked on the beach.

72
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:52,250
And now we're on the road.

73
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,000
What does it mean for you?

74
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,900
This is faith and belief.

75
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:57,950
There are so many miracles happening
there.

76
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,100
Those who take part in this find something
in it.

77
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,500
Some happiness.

78
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:08,250
And it's not only people walking.

79
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:09,500
There are also those who don't walk.

80
00:04:10,170 --> 00:04:12,450
At the side of the road, with big pots and
glasses of water.

81
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:15,150
They give food and drink to anyone passing
by.

82
00:04:15,750 --> 00:04:16,850
Without asking for anything in return.

83
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:20,350
Some pray, some watch from their homes,
some offer water,

84
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:21,650
and some are just curious.

85
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:27,650
This was a stop inside, to drink and eat
something.

86
00:04:28,350 --> 00:04:31,050
Volunteers, women and men, devoted to the
cause,

87
00:04:33,090 --> 00:04:34,450
lending a hand.

88
00:04:41,050 --> 00:04:42,300
Truly a community coming together.

89
00:04:43,050 --> 00:04:46,950
Let's try to join them for a little while,
respecting the tradition.

90
00:04:47,910 --> 00:04:49,500
The sun rises and the road doesn't empty.

91
00:05:00,570 --> 00:05:01,900
The closer you get, the slower you go.

92
00:05:13,150 --> 00:05:13,900
We made it.

93
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:29,200
Now that the whole pilgrimage is over.

94
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:32,650
In Kerala, Christianity is ancient.

95
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:36,950
Tradition says it arrived with the apostle
Thomas, in 52 AD.

96
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,200
This church was rebuilt in 1584

97
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:45,450
by an Italian Jesuit, Father Giacomo
Fenicio.

98
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:49,100
Here they still call him Veluthachan,

99
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:50,500
the white father.

100
00:05:50,710 --> 00:05:54,250
In 1647 a statue of Saint Sebastian
arrived from Milan.

101
00:05:55,140 --> 00:06:00,000
Since then Arthunkal has been a shrine, and in
January its feast brings people here from all over Kerala.

102
00:06:12,950 --> 00:06:15,950
It's boiling hot, really humid, you can
really feel it.

103
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:25,200
I came to Kerala to listen to the people
who live here.

104
00:06:25,730 --> 00:06:29,300
I found myself inside 13 kilometres, next
to people I didn't know,

105
00:06:30,030 --> 00:06:31,400
who gave us something to drink without
asking for anything.

106
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:34,400
Because travelling doesn't only mean
seeing new places.

107
00:06:35,010 --> 00:06:39,400
It also means stopping to listen to
stories we would never have known otherwise.

108
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:42,950
The journey of Voci Vere, giving a voice
to those who need it most, continues.

109
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:45,800
Follow me to discover the next stories.
